00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:44.310
So without further
ado, let's get

00:01:44.310 --> 00:01:46.360
to answering your questions.

00:01:46.360 --> 00:01:48.930
The first question
is about resveratrol.

00:01:48.930 --> 00:01:51.180
The question
specifically is, and I

00:01:51.180 --> 00:01:55.020
quote, "there seems to be a lot
of conjecture about resveratrol

00:01:55.020 --> 00:01:57.630
and whether or not it
can extend lifespan.

00:01:57.630 --> 00:02:00.900
Could you please tell us your
thoughts on this subject?"

00:02:00.900 --> 00:02:03.480
OK, well, I will indeed tell
you my thoughts on this subject.

00:02:03.480 --> 00:02:05.250
And I'll use it
as an opportunity

00:02:05.250 --> 00:02:07.980
to also give you my thoughts
about supplementation

00:02:07.980 --> 00:02:11.220
for sake of longevity, that
is, for extending lifespan,

00:02:11.220 --> 00:02:12.550
more generally.

00:02:12.550 --> 00:02:15.060
So resveratrol got
a lot of attention

00:02:15.060 --> 00:02:18.400
some years back
because, at the time,

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:21.630
it was believed that
supplementing with resveratrol

00:02:21.630 --> 00:02:25.860
could impact certain cellular
pathways that would extend not

00:02:25.860 --> 00:02:28.380
just the lifespan of
those individual cells

00:02:28.380 --> 00:02:32.490
but perhaps the lifespan of the
entire organism, meaning us,

00:02:32.490 --> 00:02:33.150
humans.

00:02:33.150 --> 00:02:34.890
And as a consequence,
supplements

00:02:34.890 --> 00:02:39.000
such as resveratrol supplements
but also grape seed extracts,

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:42.090
which we know contain a
fair amount of resveratrol

00:02:42.090 --> 00:02:44.790
or can be converted
into resveratrol, also

00:02:44.790 --> 00:02:47.250
received a lot of attention
for their potential

00:02:47.250 --> 00:02:49.510
to increase lifespan.

00:02:49.510 --> 00:02:53.220
I think by now, 2023,
it's fair to say

00:02:53.220 --> 00:02:58.110
that most of that thinking has
been, let's just say, debunked.

00:02:58.110 --> 00:03:00.360
I think that most
people understand

00:03:00.360 --> 00:03:03.180
that while indeed
resveratrol might

00:03:03.180 --> 00:03:05.940
have some positive effects on
the functioning of our cells

00:03:05.940 --> 00:03:07.770
that there is very
little, if any,

00:03:07.770 --> 00:03:11.820
direct evidence that resveratrol
can increase lifespan.

00:03:11.820 --> 00:03:16.830
If you are aware of any data
to the contrary that is modern,

00:03:16.830 --> 00:03:20.430
is highly controlled,
and even better,

00:03:20.430 --> 00:03:23.550
was carried out in human
studies or non-human primate

00:03:23.550 --> 00:03:25.620
studies or even
mouse studies, please

00:03:25.620 --> 00:03:28.258
put links to those in
the comments on YouTube,

00:03:28.258 --> 00:03:30.300
because I'd love to see
those studies, especially

00:03:30.300 --> 00:03:31.080
recent studies.

00:03:31.080 --> 00:03:33.030
But my current
line of thinking is

00:03:33.030 --> 00:03:36.480
that resveratrol while it may
have certain health benefits

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:39.390
does not seem to
increase lifespan.

00:03:39.390 --> 00:03:41.340
Now, with that
said, that doesn't

00:03:41.340 --> 00:03:43.860
mean that things like
resveratrol or grape seed

00:03:43.860 --> 00:03:45.990
extract are of zero utility.

00:03:45.990 --> 00:03:49.710
In fact, I take 400 to 800
milligrams of grape seed

00:03:49.710 --> 00:03:51.570
extract, usually with a meal.

00:03:51.570 --> 00:03:53.460
It's just part of my
standard supplementation

00:03:53.460 --> 00:03:55.470
stack every single day.

00:03:55.470 --> 00:03:58.860
But I do that mainly for its
effects on vascular function

00:03:58.860 --> 00:04:01.410
and blood flow and
a few other effects

00:04:01.410 --> 00:04:05.190
that grape seed extract
has been related to.

00:04:05.190 --> 00:04:08.190
The data there, I would say,
are reasonably strong, strong

00:04:08.190 --> 00:04:10.230
enough certainly
that when weighed

00:04:10.230 --> 00:04:13.980
against the potential downsides
of taking grape seed extract,

00:04:13.980 --> 00:04:16.620
including the cost of
grape seed extract,

00:04:16.620 --> 00:04:19.649
lead me to take 400
to 800 milligrams

00:04:19.649 --> 00:04:21.370
grape seed extract per day.

00:04:21.370 --> 00:04:24.300
I just do that as a kind
of general insurance policy

00:04:24.300 --> 00:04:25.590
against a number of things.

00:04:25.590 --> 00:04:28.230
And it's part of a
small kit of supplements

00:04:28.230 --> 00:04:30.850
that I take that fall
into that category,

00:04:30.850 --> 00:04:33.840
meaning supplements that appear
to be very safe, certainly

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:35.820
at the dosages that
I just referred to,

00:04:35.820 --> 00:04:38.550
supplements that
potentially are having

00:04:38.550 --> 00:04:41.850
positive effects on
our cells, and that are

00:04:41.850 --> 00:04:44.560
fairly if not very low cost.

00:04:44.560 --> 00:04:46.230
So that's why I take
grape seed extract.

00:04:46.230 --> 00:04:48.930
I do not take it for
its potential impact

00:04:48.930 --> 00:04:51.600
on resveratrol and
resveratrol-related pathways

00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:54.127
per se and certainly not
to extend my lifespan.

00:04:54.127 --> 00:04:56.460
So that basically answers the
question that I was asked,

00:04:56.460 --> 00:04:58.860
which is what are your
thoughts on resveratrol

00:04:58.860 --> 00:05:01.110
for extending lifespan.

00:05:01.110 --> 00:05:04.020
My answer was I don't
think it extends lifespan.

00:05:04.020 --> 00:05:07.710
But I take something related
to resveratrol for other health

00:05:07.710 --> 00:05:08.420
purposes.

00:05:08.420 --> 00:05:09.920
And by the way, I
certainly wouldn't

00:05:09.920 --> 00:05:12.860
place grape seed extract
in my list of top five

00:05:12.860 --> 00:05:15.840
or even top 10 supplements
if somebody, for instance,

00:05:15.840 --> 00:05:20.210
said I want to take anywhere
from one to 10 supplements,

00:05:20.210 --> 00:05:24.948
and I have x amount of budget
to devote to supplementation.

00:05:24.948 --> 00:05:26.990
And I'm thinking about
taking grape seed extract.

00:05:26.990 --> 00:05:28.760
Would that be one of
the top 10 supplements

00:05:28.760 --> 00:05:29.593
you would recommend?

00:05:29.593 --> 00:05:31.580
I certainly wouldn't
put it in the top 10.

00:05:31.580 --> 00:05:34.430
And by the way, at some point
in the not too distant future,

00:05:34.430 --> 00:05:36.530
I will put online--

00:05:36.530 --> 00:05:38.552
so I'll probably do a
podcast episode-- listing

00:05:38.552 --> 00:05:40.760
out all the supplements that
I take and the rationale

00:05:40.760 --> 00:05:43.135
behind those and how long I've
taken them and the effects

00:05:43.135 --> 00:05:45.770
that I've observed both
subjectively and in my blood

00:05:45.770 --> 00:05:48.062
work and what I recommend to
other people, what I don't

00:05:48.062 --> 00:05:50.103
recommend to other people,
what's specific to me,

00:05:50.103 --> 00:05:51.090
and so on and so forth.

00:05:51.090 --> 00:05:53.090
But meanwhile, that's my
answer to the question.

00:05:53.090 --> 00:05:55.370
I don't think resveratrol
increases longevity.

00:05:55.370 --> 00:05:57.590
At least, I'm not aware
of any direct evidence

00:05:57.590 --> 00:05:59.300
for that in humans.

00:05:59.300 --> 00:06:01.700
Now, with that said, let's
use this as an opportunity

00:06:01.700 --> 00:06:04.670
to talk about some of the
other so-called longevity

00:06:04.670 --> 00:06:08.130
supplements and drugs that
are often discussed online

00:06:08.130 --> 00:06:12.180
and elsewhere in terms of their
efficacy to increase lifespan.

00:06:12.180 --> 00:06:14.820
About four or five
years ago, there

00:06:14.820 --> 00:06:16.950
was a sudden and
increased attention

00:06:16.950 --> 00:06:21.730
on NAD-related pathways
for increasing longevity.

00:06:21.730 --> 00:06:25.050
So the NAD pathway, as some
of you may already know,

00:06:25.050 --> 00:06:27.540
is a pathway within
all of our cells.

00:06:27.540 --> 00:06:31.920
This is a pathway that is
highly active in young animals

00:06:31.920 --> 00:06:32.880
and humans.

00:06:32.880 --> 00:06:36.750
But all animals and humans
across the entire lifespan

00:06:36.750 --> 00:06:38.640
make NAD in their cells.

00:06:38.640 --> 00:06:41.040
It's related to
cellular energetics.

00:06:41.040 --> 00:06:43.590
That is the production
of energy in cells.

00:06:43.590 --> 00:06:45.900
It has direct relevance
to mitochondrial

00:06:45.900 --> 00:06:48.070
function and mitochondrial
function to it.

00:06:48.070 --> 00:06:50.340
And that's a
discussion unto itself.

00:06:50.340 --> 00:06:53.790
But suffice it to say that
the pathway leading to NAD

00:06:53.790 --> 00:06:57.920
includes things
such as NR and NMN.

00:06:57.920 --> 00:07:02.850
NR and NMN are considered by
many to be precursors to NAD.

00:07:02.850 --> 00:07:05.280
OK, so why am I telling
you all these acronyms?

00:07:05.280 --> 00:07:06.600
Here's the deal.

00:07:06.600 --> 00:07:09.990
The argument was made, in
fact, by some prior guests

00:07:09.990 --> 00:07:13.710
on the Huberman Lab podcast and
elsewhere that by increasing

00:07:13.710 --> 00:07:16.830
NAD levels in our cells
that one could potentially

00:07:16.830 --> 00:07:18.630
extend lifespan.

00:07:18.630 --> 00:07:21.780
And there are generally
three ways in which people

00:07:21.780 --> 00:07:23.310
have attempted to do that.

00:07:23.310 --> 00:07:26.130
OK, we'll talk about whether or
not increasing NAD in our cells

00:07:26.130 --> 00:07:27.840
actually increases
lifespan in a moment.

00:07:27.840 --> 00:07:29.940
But for the time being,
let's just talk about some

00:07:29.940 --> 00:07:32.520
of the ways that people
have tried to increase NAD

00:07:32.520 --> 00:07:34.240
within their brain and body.

00:07:34.240 --> 00:07:36.240
The most typical ways
that people have done that

00:07:36.240 --> 00:07:39.840
is through, until very
recently, supplementation.

00:07:39.840 --> 00:07:43.800
And so there are supplements
out there such as NR which we

00:07:43.800 --> 00:07:46.390
know can increase NAD levels.

00:07:46.390 --> 00:07:49.230
So this is taken as
a pill or a powder,

00:07:49.230 --> 00:07:51.570
typically as a
capsule or a powder.

00:07:51.570 --> 00:07:56.760
Or by taking NMN which,
and here there's been some,

00:07:56.760 --> 00:07:58.260
let's just say,
debate as to whether

00:07:58.260 --> 00:08:01.410
or not taking NMN actually
leads to increases

00:08:01.410 --> 00:08:03.330
in NAD within our
cells, whether or not

00:08:03.330 --> 00:08:05.038
it can get into our
cells, whether or not

00:08:05.038 --> 00:08:07.000
it's converted into NAD,
and so on and so on.

00:08:07.000 --> 00:08:10.230
But there again, the idea
was by taking NAD either

00:08:10.230 --> 00:08:12.450
in capsule form, or
it's sometimes taken

00:08:12.450 --> 00:08:15.780
as a sublingual powder, that
one could increase NAD levels

00:08:15.780 --> 00:08:19.167
and thereby potentially
increase lifespan.

00:08:19.167 --> 00:08:21.000
And then there's a third
way that's commonly

00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:22.980
used to try and
increase NAD levels,

00:08:22.980 --> 00:08:27.240
and that's by infusing
by intravenous infusion,

00:08:27.240 --> 00:08:30.840
or in some cases, by oral
administration, either liquid

00:08:30.840 --> 00:08:33.640
or pill form, NAD itself.

00:08:33.640 --> 00:08:37.980
Now, I confess that I have tried
all three of these approaches.

00:08:37.980 --> 00:08:42.299
OK, so I do indeed take an
NR supplement every day.

00:08:42.299 --> 00:08:44.880
I take 500 milligrams of NR.

00:08:44.880 --> 00:08:49.950
I also and have separately
taken an NMN supplement.

00:08:49.950 --> 00:08:51.930
I take sublingual NMN.

00:08:51.930 --> 00:08:55.020
So I'll take anywhere
from 1 to 2 grams of NMN

00:08:55.020 --> 00:08:57.280
as a sublingual powder,
which as the name suggests,

00:08:57.280 --> 00:08:59.730
you put it under your tongue,
and it dissolves there.

00:08:59.730 --> 00:09:01.680
It's got this kind
of tangy flavor.

00:09:01.680 --> 00:09:06.840
And the goal for me in taking
an NR and NMN each day--

00:09:06.840 --> 00:09:09.570
and I should mention that
sometimes I have just

00:09:09.570 --> 00:09:14.280
taken NMN or just NR to do the
comparison between NR and NMN

00:09:14.280 --> 00:09:17.280
for me in a subjective way, just
comparing what are my energy

00:09:17.280 --> 00:09:18.855
levels, how do I
feel, whether or not

00:09:18.855 --> 00:09:19.980
there are any side effects.

00:09:19.980 --> 00:09:21.605
And then I've also
taken them together.

00:09:21.605 --> 00:09:23.700
And I've arrived at a
protocol where I take

00:09:23.700 --> 00:09:26.410
NR and NMN every single day.

00:09:26.410 --> 00:09:30.150
And the goal of that is
indeed to increase NAD levels

00:09:30.150 --> 00:09:31.090
within my system.

00:09:31.090 --> 00:09:33.880
However, and I really
want to emphasize this,

00:09:33.880 --> 00:09:39.000
I do not take NR and NMN in
order to increase my lifespan.

00:09:39.000 --> 00:09:41.040
In fact, at this
point in history,

00:09:41.040 --> 00:09:45.540
it's unclear and seems somewhat
unlikely that increasing NAD is

00:09:45.540 --> 00:09:46.830
going to increase lifespan.

00:09:46.830 --> 00:09:49.980
But I think we should
always keep our minds open.

00:09:49.980 --> 00:09:52.200
There may be data to
arrive in the future that

00:09:52.200 --> 00:09:55.170
shows that actually
does happen in humans.

00:09:55.170 --> 00:09:59.190
Now, there are some animal data
suggesting that increasing NAD

00:09:59.190 --> 00:10:03.810
either by taking NR and/or
NMN can increase lifespan.

00:10:03.810 --> 00:10:06.990
But frankly, that is not
why I take NR and NMN.

00:10:06.990 --> 00:10:10.240
I take NR and NMN in an
effort to increase NAD.

00:10:10.240 --> 00:10:13.000
And now I realize what I'm about
to say is entirely subjective.

00:10:13.000 --> 00:10:14.500
And I really want
to highlight that.

00:10:14.500 --> 00:10:16.390
What I'm about to
describe is my experience.

00:10:16.390 --> 00:10:19.450
It is not based on any
peer-reviewed studies.

00:10:19.450 --> 00:10:23.170
When I take NR and
NMN at the dosages

00:10:23.170 --> 00:10:24.670
I talked about a
little bit earlier,

00:10:24.670 --> 00:10:28.028
it gives me a lot of sustained
mental and physical energy

00:10:28.028 --> 00:10:28.820
throughout the day.

00:10:28.820 --> 00:10:31.810
Now, I've always had a lot of
mental and physical energy.

00:10:31.810 --> 00:10:33.640
But I'm 48 years old now.

00:10:33.640 --> 00:10:35.650
And I'm interested
in doing anything

00:10:35.650 --> 00:10:38.710
that I safely can to keep
those levels of energy

00:10:38.710 --> 00:10:41.242
as high as is reasonable, right?

00:10:41.242 --> 00:10:42.700
I don't want to
have so much energy

00:10:42.700 --> 00:10:44.483
that I can't sit still
or so much energy

00:10:44.483 --> 00:10:45.650
that I can't sleep at night.

00:10:45.650 --> 00:10:48.770
But I find that when I take
NR and NMN in the morning--

00:10:48.770 --> 00:10:50.770
so typically, I'll do
this before my first meal.

00:10:50.770 --> 00:10:54.200
I don't really regulate how
close it is to that first meal.

00:10:54.200 --> 00:10:56.410
So I'll wake up,
use the bathroom,

00:10:56.410 --> 00:10:59.230
hydrate, get my sunlight,
do all the things I've

00:10:59.230 --> 00:11:01.000
talked about on other podcasts.

00:11:01.000 --> 00:11:03.970
But I'll take my
NR and NMN sometime

00:11:03.970 --> 00:11:05.440
usually within
about an hour or two

00:11:05.440 --> 00:11:08.620
of waking up and typically
at least 30 minutes

00:11:08.620 --> 00:11:11.330
to two hours before my first
meal, which for me usually

00:11:11.330 --> 00:11:13.400
arrives around 11:00 a.m.

00:11:13.400 --> 00:11:16.340
So sometimes I'll take it
long before my first meal.

00:11:16.340 --> 00:11:18.170
In any event, it gives
me a lot of energy.

00:11:18.170 --> 00:11:21.920
And I seem to have that
energy throughout the day.

00:11:21.920 --> 00:11:24.050
I have gone periods
of time where

00:11:24.050 --> 00:11:26.480
I stopped taking NR and/or NMN.

00:11:26.480 --> 00:11:29.870
And while I didn't feel
as if I was completely

00:11:29.870 --> 00:11:33.380
depleted of energy, I did
notice a decrement in energy

00:11:33.380 --> 00:11:35.690
compared to when
I took NR and NMN.

00:11:35.690 --> 00:11:37.670
Now, I want to be
very, very clear.

00:11:37.670 --> 00:11:40.640
I have no, zero,
financial relationship

00:11:40.640 --> 00:11:43.700
to any company that
manufactures NR.

00:11:43.700 --> 00:11:47.180
And while I used to have a
relationship to a company that

00:11:47.180 --> 00:11:50.450
made NMN, as of
recently, there's

00:11:50.450 --> 00:11:54.980
an FDA ruling that has made NMN
not available as a supplement

00:11:54.980 --> 00:11:56.430
in the wider world.

00:11:56.430 --> 00:11:59.270
So earlier this year--
that is in 2023--

00:11:59.270 --> 00:12:05.300
there was a filing for
NMN as a experimental drug

00:12:05.300 --> 00:12:06.660
in a clinical trial.

00:12:06.660 --> 00:12:12.645
And as a consequence, NMN
was listed as a banned or not

00:12:12.645 --> 00:12:14.527
allowed to be commercially
sold supplement.

00:12:14.527 --> 00:12:16.360
And that has to do with
some of the legality

00:12:16.360 --> 00:12:18.040
around clinical trials.

00:12:18.040 --> 00:12:20.500
And when something is listed
as an experimental drug,

00:12:20.500 --> 00:12:22.660
it can't be listed
as a supplement.

00:12:22.660 --> 00:12:25.930
Nonetheless, you can still
find NMN on the open market.

00:12:25.930 --> 00:12:27.273
You can find it on Amazon.

00:12:27.273 --> 00:12:28.690
I can't really
speak to the purity

00:12:28.690 --> 00:12:30.130
of one source versus another.

00:12:30.130 --> 00:12:32.330
You'll have to explore
that on your own.

00:12:32.330 --> 00:12:35.140
But I will say this, even
though I said it before.

00:12:35.140 --> 00:12:37.180
I have zero financial
relationship

00:12:37.180 --> 00:12:41.350
to any company that manufactures
and sells NMN at this time

00:12:41.350 --> 00:12:43.645
or NR at this time.

00:12:43.645 --> 00:12:45.520
So the short summary to
this whole discussion

00:12:45.520 --> 00:12:49.017
about NR and NMN is
that I take NR and NMN,

00:12:49.017 --> 00:12:51.100
but I take it because I
like how it makes me feel.

00:12:51.100 --> 00:12:53.442
It increases my energy
levels in the morning

00:12:53.442 --> 00:12:54.400
and throughout the day.

00:12:54.400 --> 00:12:55.860
And it does so in
a way that tapers

00:12:55.860 --> 00:12:57.610
off nicely in the
evening, and I can still

00:12:57.610 --> 00:12:59.030
fall asleep, et cetera.

00:12:59.030 --> 00:13:01.060
I do not take it
with any expectation

00:13:01.060 --> 00:13:02.890
that it's going to
increase my lifespan,

00:13:02.890 --> 00:13:06.100
simply because I don't think
the data substantiating

00:13:06.100 --> 00:13:08.320
the extension and
lifespan are here yet.

00:13:08.320 --> 00:13:09.630
They may arrive at some point.

00:13:09.630 --> 00:13:11.843
But I don't think that
they are here yet.

00:13:11.843 --> 00:13:13.760
So there are a good
number of people out there

00:13:13.760 --> 00:13:17.210
that still take NR and/or NMN
and are doing so in efforts

00:13:17.210 --> 00:13:18.470
to increase NAD.

00:13:18.470 --> 00:13:21.740
And so let's take a moment
and talk about increasing NAD

00:13:21.740 --> 00:13:23.965
directly, because
that's something

00:13:23.965 --> 00:13:26.090
that I have some recent
experience with, and that's

00:13:26.090 --> 00:13:30.290
becoming more common and
is, yes, still FDA approved,

00:13:30.290 --> 00:13:31.860
at least as far as I know.

00:13:31.860 --> 00:13:35.480
There are companies that
can come to your house,

00:13:35.480 --> 00:13:37.760
or you can go to a
facility, and they

00:13:37.760 --> 00:13:40.170
will give you an NAD infusion.

00:13:40.170 --> 00:13:43.100
So they will infuse you
directly with NAD into the vein.

00:13:43.100 --> 00:13:45.360
I've done this twice now.

00:13:45.360 --> 00:13:47.900
And I will say, as
most people experience

00:13:47.900 --> 00:13:51.933
when they do an NAD infusion,
it's pretty darn uncomfortable.

00:13:51.933 --> 00:13:53.600
In fact, so much so
that a lot of people

00:13:53.600 --> 00:13:57.500
have to take anti-nausea meds in
order to get the NAD infusion.

00:13:57.500 --> 00:14:00.410
I opted to not take
the anti-nausea meds,

00:14:00.410 --> 00:14:02.510
not because I'm
particularly tough,

00:14:02.510 --> 00:14:05.300
but because I don't like taking
additional medication if I can.

00:14:05.300 --> 00:14:11.150
But I've taken anywhere from
500 to 1,000 milligrams of NAD

00:14:11.150 --> 00:14:12.560
by infusion.

00:14:12.560 --> 00:14:15.290
I did that at times when
I was feeling particularly

00:14:15.290 --> 00:14:18.020
rundown or post-illness.

00:14:18.020 --> 00:14:23.030
And I did indeed find that after
the NAD infusion was complete,

00:14:23.030 --> 00:14:26.780
I felt much, much better in
a number of different ways--

00:14:26.780 --> 00:14:30.230
improved sleep, improved vigor,
coming off those illnesses.

00:14:30.230 --> 00:14:31.040
I felt much better.

00:14:31.040 --> 00:14:33.860
But again, there is
no clinical trial

00:14:33.860 --> 00:14:37.040
exploring NAD infusion
for sake of vigor,

00:14:37.040 --> 00:14:38.342
et cetera, that I am aware of.

00:14:38.342 --> 00:14:39.800
I just happen to
be somebody who is

00:14:39.800 --> 00:14:42.800
interested in exploring these
tools and techniques from time

00:14:42.800 --> 00:14:43.440
to time.

00:14:43.440 --> 00:14:44.905
And I deemed this as safe.

00:14:44.905 --> 00:14:46.280
Whether or not
it's safe for you,

00:14:46.280 --> 00:14:48.560
you have to explore
with your physician.

00:14:48.560 --> 00:14:51.140
Also, I do want to reemphasize
what I said a moment ago.

00:14:51.140 --> 00:14:54.590
Those NAD infusions are
pretty darn uncomfortable.

00:14:54.590 --> 00:14:57.470
You can have the
person administering

00:14:57.470 --> 00:15:00.360
the infusion adjust the
rate of the infusion

00:15:00.360 --> 00:15:02.090
so that the drip
is slower, which

00:15:02.090 --> 00:15:04.610
makes it more tolerable
as opposed to trying

00:15:04.610 --> 00:15:08.632
to get the whole infusion bag
in there in 45 minutes or less.

00:15:08.632 --> 00:15:10.590
I just wanted to get the
whole thing over with.

00:15:10.590 --> 00:15:13.220
So I just said, put it in
as quickly as you reasonably

00:15:13.220 --> 00:15:14.120
and safely can.

00:15:14.120 --> 00:15:17.120
It took about an hour,
maybe 45 minutes to an hour.

00:15:17.120 --> 00:15:19.040
Initially, I felt nauseous.

00:15:19.040 --> 00:15:20.990
I felt like someone was
stepping on my chest.

00:15:20.990 --> 00:15:23.450
I felt like someone was
stepping on my legs.

00:15:23.450 --> 00:15:25.850
I felt like, well,
I just felt lousy.

00:15:25.850 --> 00:15:26.990
I felt so awful.

00:15:26.990 --> 00:15:29.480
And then after about
10 minutes, it passed.

00:15:29.480 --> 00:15:30.690
And I felt fine.

00:15:30.690 --> 00:15:33.410
And then after the infusion was
done, as I mentioned before,

00:15:33.410 --> 00:15:34.580
I felt terrific.

00:15:34.580 --> 00:15:37.130
I was still able to fall
asleep that night just fine,

00:15:37.130 --> 00:15:40.310
although I did make it a point
to do this earlier in the day.

00:15:40.310 --> 00:15:42.977
I have heard of some people
doing NAD infusions later

00:15:42.977 --> 00:15:44.810
in the day and having
challenges with sleep.

00:15:44.810 --> 00:15:46.430
But again, that's
just anecdotal.

00:15:46.430 --> 00:15:49.460
Or we could call it anecdata,
if you want, but it's anecdotal.

00:15:49.460 --> 00:15:52.190
It's generally assumed
for obvious reasons

00:15:52.190 --> 00:15:56.360
that NAD infusions are more
effective at increasing

00:15:56.360 --> 00:16:01.490
cellular levels of NAD
than NR or NMN or both

00:16:01.490 --> 00:16:04.280
together, although the direct
comparison has not been made,

00:16:04.280 --> 00:16:05.165
as far as I know.

00:16:05.165 --> 00:16:07.040
And there's still this
general question as to

00:16:07.040 --> 00:16:10.670
whether or not any of this stuff
is getting into cells directly

00:16:10.670 --> 00:16:13.520
and impacting NAD levels
in specific cells,

00:16:13.520 --> 00:16:16.280
although I think most
people assume that the NAD

00:16:16.280 --> 00:16:18.110
infusions certainly are.

00:16:18.110 --> 00:16:20.510
Now, there are a number of
different experts out there

00:16:20.510 --> 00:16:23.440
who debate all the fine points
of everything that I just said,

00:16:23.440 --> 00:16:25.190
people like Dr. Charles
Brenner and people

00:16:25.190 --> 00:16:28.160
like Dr. David Sinclair,
people like Matt Kaeberlein.

00:16:28.160 --> 00:16:30.080
There are people
who really actively,

00:16:30.080 --> 00:16:33.350
and let's just say, heatedly
debate all the issues

00:16:33.350 --> 00:16:35.240
that I just talked about.

00:16:35.240 --> 00:16:38.060
I think the greatest debate
is around whether or not

00:16:38.060 --> 00:16:41.750
increasing NAD levels in cells
actually increases lifespan.

00:16:41.750 --> 00:16:43.760
But there's also a debate
around whether or not

00:16:43.760 --> 00:16:47.480
NR is more advantageous than
NMN, whether or not all of this

00:16:47.480 --> 00:16:50.030
is too premature to
explore yet already.

00:16:50.030 --> 00:16:52.640
Again, I just want to
restate for the third time.

00:16:52.640 --> 00:16:55.820
I don't do any of this
stuff in these NAD pathways

00:16:55.820 --> 00:16:58.040
for sake of increasing lifespan.

00:16:58.040 --> 00:17:01.370
I do it for sake of the
vitality and energy effects

00:17:01.370 --> 00:17:03.710
that I subjectively experience.

00:17:03.710 --> 00:17:07.849
I must say that the NAD
infusions are expensive enough,

00:17:07.849 --> 00:17:12.530
inconvenient enough, and let's
just say uncomfortable enough

00:17:12.530 --> 00:17:15.800
that I don't see myself
doing them very often,

00:17:15.800 --> 00:17:19.280
although perhaps maybe doing
them a couple of times a year

00:17:19.280 --> 00:17:21.560
or more makes sense
should I find myself

00:17:21.560 --> 00:17:24.810
feeling run down or post-illness
fatigue or things of that sort.

00:17:24.810 --> 00:17:27.560
I would be very curious
to learn from any of you,

00:17:27.560 --> 00:17:29.780
the audience, what
sorts of things

00:17:29.780 --> 00:17:32.240
you've experienced
if perhaps you've

00:17:32.240 --> 00:17:35.540
explored NR supplementation,
NMN supplementation, or NAD

00:17:35.540 --> 00:17:36.380
infusions.

00:17:36.380 --> 00:17:37.880
And as I mentioned
earlier, there's

00:17:37.880 --> 00:17:39.920
now a growing number
of different products

00:17:39.920 --> 00:17:43.580
that claim that you
can take NAD orally,

00:17:43.580 --> 00:17:45.800
so either in pill,
tincture or other forms,

00:17:45.800 --> 00:17:48.110
so no requirement
for an infusion.

00:17:48.110 --> 00:17:51.140
But I'm not aware of any
studies that have directly

00:17:51.140 --> 00:17:55.250
linked oral NAD to
NAD levels in cells

00:17:55.250 --> 00:17:56.840
and how those two things relate.

00:17:56.840 --> 00:18:00.860
So lots more important science
to be done in this area, lots

00:18:00.860 --> 00:18:03.752
more debate surely to
be had, and any time we

00:18:03.752 --> 00:18:05.210
talk about supplements,
I just want

00:18:05.210 --> 00:18:09.590
to emphasize several times that
I do see supplements as indeed

00:18:09.590 --> 00:18:10.160
supplements.

00:18:10.160 --> 00:18:12.440
I think only by getting your
light exposure, sunshine,

00:18:12.440 --> 00:18:14.870
movement, nutrition,
stress modulation,

00:18:14.870 --> 00:18:18.020
social relationships, et
cetera, correct should you even

00:18:18.020 --> 00:18:19.790
begin to consider
supplementation,

00:18:19.790 --> 00:18:22.220
because supplementation
is just not

00:18:22.220 --> 00:18:24.523
at the foundation of mental
health, physical health,

00:18:24.523 --> 00:18:25.190
and performance.

00:18:25.190 --> 00:18:27.260
It is indeed something
that, provided

00:18:27.260 --> 00:18:30.590
it fits within your safety
and economic frameworks,

00:18:30.590 --> 00:18:32.610
could potentially
enhance mental health,

00:18:32.610 --> 00:18:34.730
physical health,
performance in certain ways.

00:18:34.730 --> 00:18:36.503
But it's certainly
not the foundation

00:18:36.503 --> 00:18:38.670
from which you build mental
health, physical health,

00:18:38.670 --> 00:18:39.660
and performance.

00:18:39.660 --> 00:18:42.050
So now we've talked about
resveratrol, a little bit

00:18:42.050 --> 00:18:43.130
about grape seed extract.

00:18:43.130 --> 00:18:46.850
We've talked about NR and NMN
and NAD and the NAD pathway.

00:18:46.850 --> 00:18:49.250
There are a few other
things that are commonly

00:18:49.250 --> 00:18:53.510
discussed in the longevity
sphere, let's call

00:18:53.510 --> 00:18:56.420
it, things such as metformin.

00:18:56.420 --> 00:18:59.930
I'll just be very direct and
say I do not take metformin.

00:18:59.930 --> 00:19:01.708
And I also don't
take what some people

00:19:01.708 --> 00:19:04.250
call the poor man's version of
metformin, which is berberine.

00:19:04.250 --> 00:19:06.140
Berberine gives me
brutal headaches.

00:19:06.140 --> 00:19:07.940
Berberine lowers blood glucose.

00:19:07.940 --> 00:19:10.550
That's why I think it's
giving me brutal headaches.

00:19:10.550 --> 00:19:13.130
A lot of people
have explored or are

00:19:13.130 --> 00:19:16.220
thinking about exploring taking
metformin or berberine for sake

00:19:16.220 --> 00:19:20.540
of lowering blood glucose and
lowering a particular cellular,

00:19:20.540 --> 00:19:23.960
let's just say, pathway or
a set of molecules, mTOR

00:19:23.960 --> 00:19:26.450
being the most common of them.

00:19:26.450 --> 00:19:28.400
mTOR, mammalian
Target of Rapamycin,

00:19:28.400 --> 00:19:30.920
is abundant in developing cells.

00:19:30.920 --> 00:19:33.320
It's responsible for the
growth of individual cells.

00:19:33.320 --> 00:19:35.750
And the amount of
mTOR in our cells

00:19:35.750 --> 00:19:37.940
tapers off across our lifespan.

00:19:37.940 --> 00:19:39.852
mTOR and its
pathways is something

00:19:39.852 --> 00:19:41.810
that I've actually worked
on fairly extensively

00:19:41.810 --> 00:19:44.750
in my laboratory in the
context of the regeneration

00:19:44.750 --> 00:19:46.290
of the visual system.

00:19:46.290 --> 00:19:47.750
So I'm very familiar with it.

00:19:47.750 --> 00:19:50.900
And for sake of convenience
and ease in this conversation,

00:19:50.900 --> 00:19:52.490
we can just think
of mTOR as something

00:19:52.490 --> 00:19:55.130
that's abundant in
cells during development

00:19:55.130 --> 00:19:57.500
and any time cells
are growing, including

00:19:57.500 --> 00:20:01.070
the growth of tumor
cells, and cellular growth

00:20:01.070 --> 00:20:03.180
at any stage of the lifespan.

00:20:03.180 --> 00:20:06.020
So the logic that
people have waged

00:20:06.020 --> 00:20:09.860
is that drugs like metformin
or compounds like berberine

00:20:09.860 --> 00:20:14.480
that reduce mTOR levels or
impact the mTOR pathway in ways

00:20:14.480 --> 00:20:17.150
that lead to net
decreases in mTOR,

00:20:17.150 --> 00:20:21.050
the logic is that could
somehow increase lifespan.

00:20:21.050 --> 00:20:23.720
There's also the logic that
fasting can reduce mTOR

00:20:23.720 --> 00:20:25.110
which can increase lifespan.

00:20:25.110 --> 00:20:27.193
I don't think there's any
direct evidence for that

00:20:27.193 --> 00:20:29.310
yet, however, at
least not in humans.

00:20:29.310 --> 00:20:30.440
So I'll tell you.

00:20:30.440 --> 00:20:33.430
I don't take berberine for the
reasons I mentioned before.

00:20:33.430 --> 00:20:35.090
It makes me feel uncomfortable.

00:20:35.090 --> 00:20:36.530
Not psychologically
uncomfortable,

00:20:36.530 --> 00:20:38.280
it makes me feel
physically uncomfortable.

00:20:38.280 --> 00:20:42.170
I don't take metformin because
expert colleagues of mine,

00:20:42.170 --> 00:20:45.450
including Dr. Peter Attia,
have come on this podcast.

00:20:45.450 --> 00:20:47.990
In fact, we did a collaboration
journal club podcast

00:20:47.990 --> 00:20:49.657
that we'll provide a
link to in the show

00:20:49.657 --> 00:20:52.340
note captions during which
we, meaning mainly Peter,

00:20:52.340 --> 00:20:56.690
reviewed the peer-reviewed
data on metformin and lifespan.

00:20:56.690 --> 00:20:59.570
And at least to
my understanding,

00:20:59.570 --> 00:21:02.150
at present, there
isn't sufficient data

00:21:02.150 --> 00:21:06.990
to support taking metformin
for increasing lifespan.

00:21:06.990 --> 00:21:08.400
So that's why I don't take it.

00:21:08.400 --> 00:21:11.280
I may in the future if more
data come out and things change.

00:21:11.280 --> 00:21:14.460
But right now, I see no
reason to take metformin

00:21:14.460 --> 00:21:16.330
to increase my lifespan.

00:21:16.330 --> 00:21:18.120
So I don't take metformin.

00:21:18.120 --> 00:21:20.190
Similarly, there's
a lot of discussion

00:21:20.190 --> 00:21:21.780
out there about rapamycin.

00:21:21.780 --> 00:21:25.110
Remember mTOR, mammalian
Target of Rapamycin,

00:21:25.110 --> 00:21:27.900
is so named because it's a
target of this drug, which

00:21:27.900 --> 00:21:30.120
is used largely as
an anticancer drug

00:21:30.120 --> 00:21:31.800
but has other purposes as well.

00:21:31.800 --> 00:21:34.710
Rapamycin is actively
under investigation,

00:21:34.710 --> 00:21:36.960
which makes it sound like
there was a crime committed.

00:21:36.960 --> 00:21:39.630
But as far as I
know, there wasn't.

00:21:39.630 --> 00:21:42.360
Under active
scientific exploration

00:21:42.360 --> 00:21:44.280
would be the more
accurate way to say it,

00:21:44.280 --> 00:21:47.640
by excellent researchers such
as Dr. Matt Kaeberlein up

00:21:47.640 --> 00:21:49.800
at the University of
Washington in Seattle.

00:21:49.800 --> 00:21:51.900
He's been looking at
rapamycin for its ability

00:21:51.900 --> 00:21:55.270
to extend lifespan, focusing
on many different species,

00:21:55.270 --> 00:21:56.190
including dogs.

00:21:56.190 --> 00:21:58.410
So he has a dog
longevity project.

00:21:58.410 --> 00:21:59.970
So that's really interesting.

00:21:59.970 --> 00:22:02.580
Dr. Peter Attia has talked
a lot about rapamycin

00:22:02.580 --> 00:22:04.890
and did a recent
podcast about rapamycin

00:22:04.890 --> 00:22:07.830
with not only Matt
Kaeberlein but one

00:22:07.830 --> 00:22:09.840
of the experts in
the world on mTOR.

00:22:09.840 --> 00:22:12.360
So I invite you to check
out that podcast if you

00:22:12.360 --> 00:22:13.860
want to learn about rapamycin.

00:22:13.860 --> 00:22:15.810
So there is a fair
amount of understanding

00:22:15.810 --> 00:22:19.800
about the biological pathways
of rapamycin and mTOR and so on.

00:22:19.800 --> 00:22:22.620
And there are
clinician physicians,

00:22:22.620 --> 00:22:25.350
like Peter as well
as others, who

00:22:25.350 --> 00:22:28.770
are quite excited about
the potential for rapamycin

00:22:28.770 --> 00:22:31.290
to extend lifespan, although
you have to go directly

00:22:31.290 --> 00:22:33.310
to Peter to find out
exactly what he's doing,

00:22:33.310 --> 00:22:35.490
whether or not he's
taking rapamycin or not.

00:22:35.490 --> 00:22:37.260
I certainly can't speak for him.

00:22:37.260 --> 00:22:40.710
But at present, I
don't take rapamycin.

00:22:40.710 --> 00:22:42.420
Why don't I take rapamycin?

00:22:42.420 --> 00:22:47.010
Well, I don't take rapamycin
because at least to my eye,

00:22:47.010 --> 00:22:49.590
the data at present
don't justify

00:22:49.590 --> 00:22:52.080
that for sake of
increasing lifespan.

00:22:52.080 --> 00:22:53.460
That is not to
say that rapamycin

00:22:53.460 --> 00:22:56.580
isn't an effective drug for the
treatment of various cancers

00:22:56.580 --> 00:22:57.550
and for other purposes.

00:22:57.550 --> 00:23:00.010
But for me, at
this point in time,

00:23:00.010 --> 00:23:03.630
I just don't see a
good reason for me

00:23:03.630 --> 00:23:07.760
to take rapamycin relative to
some of the, let's just say,

00:23:07.760 --> 00:23:10.580
substantiated potential
side effects of rapamycin.

00:23:10.580 --> 00:23:13.640
It is a drug that I
think can be taken safely

00:23:13.640 --> 00:23:17.900
under certain conditions but has
enough of a side effect profile

00:23:17.900 --> 00:23:19.970
that I'm not
interested in taking it

00:23:19.970 --> 00:23:22.740
for sake of increasing
lifespan at this time.

00:23:22.740 --> 00:23:26.270
So no metformin, no
rapamycin for me right now,

00:23:26.270 --> 00:23:27.530
perhaps in the future.

00:23:27.530 --> 00:23:29.240
I've listed out
the things that I'm

00:23:29.240 --> 00:23:32.960
perfectly willing and happy
to do, grape seed extract, NR

00:23:32.960 --> 00:23:36.920
and NMN, the
occasional NAD infusion

00:23:36.920 --> 00:23:39.680
to increase NAD directly,
and for the time being,

00:23:39.680 --> 00:23:42.703
I've decided to stay away
from metformin and rapamycin.

00:23:42.703 --> 00:23:44.120
But of course, any
and all of that

00:23:44.120 --> 00:23:45.620
could change going
forward depending

00:23:45.620 --> 00:23:49.070
on the data that are published
and my own experiences.

00:23:49.070 --> 00:23:52.760
As a final point on this,
I want to again emphasize

00:23:52.760 --> 00:23:57.320
that the foundation of a
quality life and a long life

00:23:57.320 --> 00:24:01.520
is most certainly going to
come from the basics, perhaps

00:24:01.520 --> 00:24:03.380
the most fundamental
and important of which

00:24:03.380 --> 00:24:06.110
is to get sufficient amounts
of quality sleep each night.

00:24:06.110 --> 00:24:08.400
We know that not
doing that can indeed

00:24:08.400 --> 00:24:11.940
reduce your lifespan if not
directly, then certainly

00:24:11.940 --> 00:24:14.220
indirectly by increased
number of accidents

00:24:14.220 --> 00:24:17.160
and certainly being far
less happy and energetic

00:24:17.160 --> 00:24:17.830
during the day.

00:24:17.830 --> 00:24:19.080
So that's fundamental.

00:24:19.080 --> 00:24:21.960
Also, and this is very
important to emphasize--

00:24:21.960 --> 00:24:24.750
and here I'm essentially
borrowing the words straight

00:24:24.750 --> 00:24:27.100
out of Dr. Peter Attia's mouth.

00:24:27.100 --> 00:24:28.740
So forgive me, Peter.

00:24:28.740 --> 00:24:30.720
This won't be nearly
as eloquent or succinct

00:24:30.720 --> 00:24:31.980
as Peter would make it.

00:24:31.980 --> 00:24:35.220
But it is very, very clear
that at present there

00:24:35.220 --> 00:24:38.580
is no supplement or drug
for increasing longevity

00:24:38.580 --> 00:24:43.290
that even comes close to the
known improvements in health

00:24:43.290 --> 00:24:46.710
metrics that relate to longevity
that come from getting quality

00:24:46.710 --> 00:24:49.890
sleep and especially from
getting sufficient amounts

00:24:49.890 --> 00:24:51.790
of quality exercise.

00:24:51.790 --> 00:24:55.410
So that means both a combination
of cardiovascular exercise,

00:24:55.410 --> 00:25:01.320
a minimum of 180 to 220 minutes
of so-called zone 2 cardio

00:25:01.320 --> 00:25:02.815
per week.

00:25:02.815 --> 00:25:04.440
So that's cardio that
you can carry out

00:25:04.440 --> 00:25:06.060
while still maintaining
a conversation

00:25:06.060 --> 00:25:08.330
but should you increase
the intensity any more,

00:25:08.330 --> 00:25:11.130
you would have a hard time
completing your sentences.

00:25:11.130 --> 00:25:13.727
But in addition to that also
doing some VO2 max work,

00:25:13.727 --> 00:25:16.310
so getting your heart rate way,
way up at least once per week,

00:25:16.310 --> 00:25:19.490
and also, of course, doing
resistance training either

00:25:19.490 --> 00:25:21.800
with weights, machines
or bodyweight,

00:25:21.800 --> 00:25:23.870
doing that at
sufficient intensity,

00:25:23.870 --> 00:25:27.500
six sets minimum per
body part per week

00:25:27.500 --> 00:25:30.530
to maintain not just
muscular size and strength

00:25:30.530 --> 00:25:33.740
but equally important,
perhaps even more important,

00:25:33.740 --> 00:25:36.390
maintaining nerve to
muscle connectivity,

00:25:36.390 --> 00:25:38.510
which correlates with
cognitive function

00:25:38.510 --> 00:25:40.760
and a number of other
important longevity metrics.

00:25:40.760 --> 00:25:45.920
So again exercise, sleep,
quality nutrition, quality

00:25:45.920 --> 00:25:48.080
social connection,
which means eliminating

00:25:48.080 --> 00:25:50.870
as best you can toxic
social connection

00:25:50.870 --> 00:25:53.690
and increasing quality social
connection, people that you

00:25:53.690 --> 00:25:56.450
like and enjoy spending time
with and feel enriched by,

00:25:56.450 --> 00:25:59.180
stress modulation, all of
these things are so key.

00:25:59.180 --> 00:26:01.940
And of course, getting morning
sunlight, all of those things

00:26:01.940 --> 00:26:06.140
combine to have a huge out-sized
effect compared to anything

00:26:06.140 --> 00:26:09.250
that you could take in
pill, capsule or infusion.

00:26:09.250 --> 00:26:11.820
So before even considering
taking any supplement or drug

00:26:11.820 --> 00:26:15.780
to increase your longevity or
even for increasing vitality

00:26:15.780 --> 00:26:19.290
for that matter, get those
basics of sleep, sunlight,

00:26:19.290 --> 00:26:22.800
nutrition, movement, stress
modulation, or stress control,

00:26:22.800 --> 00:26:25.920
I should say, and
relationships down.

00:26:25.920 --> 00:26:26.642
Get those right.

00:26:26.642 --> 00:26:29.100
And get that morning sunlight
to set your circadian rhythm,

00:26:29.100 --> 00:26:30.767
because of course,
your circadian rhythm

00:26:30.767 --> 00:26:32.190
is what anchors it all.

00:26:32.190 --> 00:26:35.220
And I'd be completely
remiss if I didn't emphasize

00:26:35.220 --> 00:26:38.970
yet again that any time you're
thinking of adding a supplement

00:26:38.970 --> 00:26:41.040
or removing a supplement
from your regimen

00:26:41.040 --> 00:26:44.400
or adding a prescription drug
or removing a prescription drug,

00:26:44.400 --> 00:26:47.160
you absolutely
should consult you're

00:26:47.160 --> 00:26:49.020
board-certified physician.

